+Start exploring (``p``)
+  With the :ref:`Autoexplore Commands Option <autoexplore-commands-option>`
+  enabled and no monsters in view, ``p`` rests as needed (like ``R`` followed
+  by ``&``), then follows known routes to unexplored parts of the level.
+  You can cross glyphs of warding and open doors along the way. If you fail
+  to pick a lock, exploration stops and skips that door on later attempts
+  until you see it open or the terrain change. Routes avoid damaging terrain,
+  impassable rubble, and known traps that can affect you.
+
+  Exploration stops with "Something is here." when you notice a monster,
+  staircase, trap, secret door, or new item on the floor. Treasure and
+  ignored items do not interrupt exploration. Several discoveries on the same
+  step give one message. Pressing ``p`` again lets you pass items you have
+  already seen. When you step on them, the usual pickup rules apply,
+  including limits such as ``=g5``. Other disturbances can also stop exploration.
+  Press Escape to interrupt resting or movement, and ``p`` to explore again.
 
